  "data": {
    "email-intake:17c7bcda-2f96-4a89-9fb1-74dc30b32baa": {
      "size": 971,
      "value": "{\"intakeId\":\"17c7bcda-2f96-4a89-9fb1-74dc30b32baa\",\"from\":\"jaco_sun@163.com\",\"to\":\"bot@misakanet.org\",\"subject\":\"=?utf-8?b?5ZKM5Yip5pe26ZuG5Zui54Ot5oub77ya5pm66IO95L2T5byA5Y+R5bel56iL5biI?=\",\"intakeType\":\"unknown\",\"lessonContent\":\"Ikalus1988 你好，\\n\\n我在 GitHub 上看到你在 MisakaNet 上的工作，尤其是 mcp 相关的实践，\\n和我们正在做的事高度契合，想和你简单聊聊。\\n\\n我们是和利时科技集团，国内工业自动化解决方案头部企业，正在北京、西安组建\\n「智能体运行时团队」，技术负责人直接带教，适合想往底层 Agent 工程方向深耕的人。\\n\\n岗位：智能体开发工程师（北京/西安，3 人，接受应届）\\n\\n你将负责：\\n- LangGraph/LangChain 主链编排：意图理解、模型调用编排、结果写回闭环\\n- Blackboard 共享工作记忆：多步骤中间结果的结构化存储与读写权限\\n- Harness 五层护栏：指令注入 / 状态机 / 权限范围 / 输出校验 / 会话生命周期\\n- MCP 工具集成、SSE/WebSocket 流式通信、可回溯 trace\\n\\n我们希望你：\\n- 熟练 LangChain/LangGraph，做过项目级设计（不是只跑示例）\\n- 掌握 function calling / 结构化输出 / 上下文窗口管理\\n- 熟练 asyncio + FastAPI，具备持久化与 API 集成能力\\n- 加分：DPO/RLHF、LLM-as-a-Judge、工业/制造/能源业务经验\\n\\n如果你近期有看机会的想法，欢迎把简历发送至 ghrtraining@hollysys.com；\\n即使暂时没有，也期待能认识一下，以后说不定有合作机会。\\n\\n期待回复。\",\"nodeId\":\"Misaka10062\",\"receivedAt\":\"2026-08-19T08:49:40.544Z\",\"status\":\"processed\"}"
    },
    "email-intake:4f261095-c700-4836-abef-5fcf9c5d8d55": {
      "size": 2910,
      "value": "{\"intakeId\":\"4f261095-c700-4836-abef-5fcf9c5d8d55\",\"from\":\"yifan@dao42.com\",\"to\":\"bot@misakanet.org\",\"subject\":\"=?utf-8?B?V2hhdCBzaG91bGQgeW91ciBBSSBhZ2VudCBiZWNv?= =?utf-8?B?bWU/Cgo=?=\",\"intakeType\":\"unknown\",\"lessonContent\":\"Hi,\\n\\nI’m Yifan from the founding team at OpenClacky. We came through MiraclePlus, founded by the former YC China team.\\n\\nMost AI agents are shipped as finished products. The company decides their tools, interface, and workflow, and users adapt to those choices.\\n\\nWe think an agent should work the other way around.\\n\\nOpenClacky is an open-source, local-first AI agent built around a stable core and an extensible software layer.\\n\\nThe core handles models, files, sessions, tools, context, and permissions. Everything that makes the product yours can live in extensions: Skills, specialized Agents, UI panels, APIs, channels, hooks, and even changes to runtime behavior.\\n\\nYou do not need to know which component to build. Describe what you want in plain language—an Obsidian-style knowledge workspace, a research system, a content studio, or a multi-agent team—and the Extension Developer Agent can plan, build, verify, and load it into your existing OpenClacky.\\n\\nYour files, sessions, and context stay where they are. The Agent simply grows the software you need around them.\\n\\nA workflow can start as a Skill. As it gets used, it can grow its own interface, data, identity, and backend, eventually becoming software that others can install, modify, and adapt.\\n\\nThat is the ecosystem we are building: developers contribute integrations, domain experts contribute proven methods, users contribute real problems, and the Agent helps turn all three into working products.\\n\\nOur job is not to decide what OpenClacky should become for everyone. Our job is to keep the core reliable and extensible, while the people who actually use it decide what it grows into.\\n\\nUnderneath, OpenClacky remains MIT-licensed, local-first, model-flexible, and intentionally lean. Prompt caching, context compression, and a small core make long-running, evolving Agents practical—but they are the foundation, not the destination.\\n\\nWebsite: https://www.openclacky.com/\\nGitHub: https://github.com/clacky-ai/openclacky\\n\\nIf there is a workflow you repeat, a part of your current Agent that feels limiting, or a piece of software you wish it could become, we would love to see you build it with us.\\n\\nBest,\\nYifan\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n                        \\n                                                                        深圳至简天成科技                                                                                                                                                                          \\n                                                                                                    杨一帆\",\"nodeId\":\"Misaka10063\",\"receivedAt\":\"2026-08-20T09:02:24.567Z\",\"status\":\"processed\"}"
    },
    "email-intake:b151ddb8-2ca8-45a8-823b-01232ba57f04": {
      "size": 1430,
      "value": "{\"intakeId\":\"b151ddb8-2ca8-45a8-823b-01232ba57f04\",\"from\":\"hello@trymcpvault.com\",\"to\":\"bot@misakanet.org\",\"subject\":\"MisakaNet is listed on MCPVault\",\"intakeType\":\"unknown\",\"lessonContent\":\"Hi misakanet-bot,\\n\\nI run MCPVault, a directory of MCP servers with quality signals:\\nlast-commit recency, live verification, client compatibility. It was\\nrecently voted Product of the Day on Fazier.\\n\\nWhile indexing GitHub I picked up MisakaNet, so it already has a listing here:\\n\\nhttps://mcpvault.io/servers/misakanet\\n\\nRight now it only shows the basic GitHub facts. If you want, you can\\nclaim it and take control of the listing: description, category,\\ncompatibility tags, install command. Claiming is free, you sign in\\nwith GitHub, and it takes about a minute.\\n\\nClaimed servers can also request verification. We actually spin up the\\nserver, run a real MCP handshake, and if it passes you get a Verified\\nbadge plus a do-follow link to your site. Verification is free during\\nearly access.\\n\\nNo catch, the listing exists either way. I just think maintainers\\nshould hear about it from me rather than find it by accident.\\n\\nReply if you have any questions, I read every answer myself.\\n\\nHenrik\\nMCPVault, https://mcpvault.io\\n\\nIf you would rather not hear from me again, just reply \\\"unsubscribe\\\"\\nand I will not email you after that.\",\"nodeId\":\"Misaka10109\",\"receivedAt\":\"2026-08-31T07:32:51.154Z\",\"status\":\"processed\"}"
    },
    "email-intake:ca2c8b1c-889c-4da4-bccf-e6ce3f15c422": {
      "size": 1391,
      "value": "{\"intakeId\":\"ca2c8b1c-889c-4da4-bccf-e6ce3f15c422\",\"from\":\"hello@trymcpvault.com\",\"to\":\"bot@misakanet.org\",\"subject\":\"Re: MisakaNet is listed on MCPVault (last note)\",\"intakeType\":\"unknown\",\"lessonContent\":\"Hi misakanet-bot,\\n\\nLast one from me, promise. If the listing is not something you care\\nabout right now, all good, it will simply stay as an unclaimed entry\\nwith the basic GitHub facts.\\n\\nA few things worth keeping in your back pocket:\\n\\n1. The claim link does not expire:\\nhttps://mcpvault.io/servers/misakanet. Free, GitHub sign-in, about a\\nminute.\\n2. Verification is free during early access. Servers that pass the\\nlive MCP handshake keep the Verified badge and the do-follow link as\\nlong as they keep passing.\\n3. Claimed servers get a weekly security profile (NVIDIA SkillSpector,\\nstatic): what the code reaches and any dependencies with advisories,\\nno grade, with the full list and fixes in the dashboard. Handy for\\nspotting a vulnerable dependency before a user does.\\n4. If you ever want to check that MisakaNet still speaks MCP\\ncorrectly, the tester at https://mcpvault.io/test runs a real\\nhandshake and shows you exactly what a client sees. Free, no sign-in.\\n\\nGood luck with MisakaNet,\\nHenrik\\nMCPVault, https://mcpvault.io\\n\\nTo stop these emails, reply \\\"unsubscribe\\\".\",\"nodeId\":\"Misaka10109\",\"receivedAt\":\"2026-09-07T07:02:17.249Z\",\"status\":\"processed\"}"
    },
    "email-intake:e0e5c9ac-3279-4295-96ed-244bc1a1d897": {
      "size": 1171,
      "value": "{\"intakeId\":\"e0e5c9ac-3279-4295-96ed-244bc1a1d897\",\"from\":\"hello@trymcpvault.com\",\"to\":\"bot@misakanet.org\",\"subject\":\"Re: MisakaNet is listed on MCPVault\",\"intakeType\":\"unknown\",\"lessonContent\":\"Hi misakanet-bot,\\n\\nJust following up on my note from a few days ago, in case it got buried.\\n\\nShort version: MisakaNet is already listed at\\nhttps://mcpvault.io/servers/misakanet. Claiming it is free (GitHub\\nsign-in, about a minute) and gives you control of the listing. If you\\nthen request verification and the server passes a real MCP handshake,\\nyou get the Verified badge and a do-follow link to your site.\\nVerification is free during early access.\\n\\nThe badge is also embeddable in your README, so people checking out\\nyour repo can see the server is tested and working. MCPVault was\\nrecently voted Product of the Day on Fazier, so the badge is a signal\\npeople are starting to recognize.\\n\\nAny questions, just reply. And if this is not relevant, tell me and I\\nwill not follow up again.\\n\\nHenrik\\nMCPVault, https://mcpvault.io\\n\\nTo stop these emails, reply \\\"unsubscribe\\\".\",\"nodeId\":\"Misaka10109\",\"receivedAt\":\"2026-09-03T07:08:43.119Z\",\"status\":\"processed\"}"
    },
